'' A STATIC or SHARED float initialiser folds a NAMED constant and ATN. Three gaps, one
'' statement in starshine.bas -- 'static as _float ang = type( 0, .2, pi2 / 2 )' after
'' 'const pi2 = 4 * atn( 1 )' in the same procedure -- which declined:
''
''   - the float folder was handed no scope, so no named constant folded -- and a SCALAR
''     static then fell to the integer folder, whose answer a float global never reads:
''     'static as single z = kk' was 0 where fbc prints 3, with nothing declined;
''   - a const declared in the procedure's BODY is not visible from procScope, so the
''     static's own scope (VarScopeOf_) is what the aggregate fold now starts from;
''   - ATN was not folded at all. It is a libm answer, so it was MEASURED: fbc-modern's
''     folded image of the arrays below, printed as bits, against tiko's -- all 26 equal.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 -gen gcc -r:
''
''     static struct $2F3 ANG$1 = { 0x0p+0f, 0x1.99999Ap-3f, 0x1.921FB6p+0f };
''     static float Z$1 = 0x1.8p+1f;
''     static double H$1 = 0x1.8p+0;
''
'' -- and the images below are those values, little-endian.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/static-float-const-init.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var agg PLANET$ang size 12 = bytes 00 00 00 00 CD CC 4C 3E DB 0F C9 3F
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var f32 SCALAR$z = 3
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var f64 SCALAR$h = 1.5
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var agg a size 160 = bytes 18 2D 44 54 FB 21 E9 3F 18 2D 44 54 FB 21 E9 BF 4F BB 61 05 67 AC DD 3F 44 BE EB 92 E1 B6 F1 3F 4D CC E2 82 E2 83 B9 3F 54 00 16 2C BD 89 F7 3F 22 EF 2D EB 05 F9 F8 3F 3A 8C 30 E2 8E 79 45 3E 3C FB 94 51 FB 21 F9 3F 60 85 7A 6B 17 FC F3 3F DD 80 2C F9 75 5B CF 3F E1 9E 26 A3 8F 97 E4 3F 9B F6 81 D2 0B 73 EF 3F 06 AF 1E 66 3A A7 D2 BF 18 2D 44 54 FB 21 F9 3F A0 3F 8C 3A E2 1D E9 3F 84 A0 8C 61 13 26 E9 3F 60 85 7A 6B 17 FC F3 3F 18 2D 44 54 FB 21 09 40 E1 9E 26 A3 8F 97 D4 3F
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var agg b size 24 = bytes DB 0F 49 3F DB 0F C9 3F 14 1F CC 3D 2C E6 B6 3F 6C 5B 98 BF BB E0 9F 3F
